{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Cart icon bubble (render target)
  Phase 8. This section is never placed in a template or a section group. It
  exists so the Section Rendering API has something with a STABLE id to return.

  A section placed in a JSON template is given a generated id such as
  sections--1234__header, which changes; a section file rendered on its own
  keeps its filename as its id, so assets/cart.js can ask for
  "cart-icon-bubble" by name and never have to discover it at runtime.

  It carries no schema deliberately. It needs no settings — a standalone render
  target cannot receive them, the docs are explicit that it would fall back to
  defaults — and it must not appear in the merchant's Add section list, which
  is what a preset would do. enabled_on / disabled_on are omitted for the same
  reason: their interaction with the Rendering API is undocumented, and leaving
  them off removes the question.

  Its entire body is the same snippet sections/header.liquid renders inline, so
  the swapped markup and the server-rendered markup cannot drift apart.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'cart-icon-bubble' %}
